quartz-wm: _NET_WM_MOVERESIZE and the EWMH frameless clients need

Applies after quartz-wm-picture.patch (scripts/build-xquartz.sh step 5).

Frameless X clients draw their own title bar and ask the window manager to
run interactive moves/resizes with the EWMH _NET_WM_MOVERESIZE client
message; quartz-wm neither advertised nor handled it, so those windows could
not be moved or resized at all. SDL3 hit-test windows send it from
X11_TriggerHitTestAction, Chromium/CEF custom frames from
X11Window::DispatchHostWindowDragMovement (ui::DoWMMoveResize, button 0).
Steam (CEF "System" composer) nests the two: SDL3 toplevel (Motif
decorations = 0) -> CefWindowX11 -> Chromium X11Window, which selects
ButtonPress. Chromium gets every press, SDL's hit test never runs, and any
request names Chromium's window, two levels below the managed one.

* _NET_WM_MOVERESIZE: directions 0-7 (edge/corner resize) and 8 (move),
  11 (cancel: ends the drag where it is); 9/10 (keyboard) ignored. A
  request for a window inside a managed one (up to 8 levels down) applies
  to that one. Runs on X pointer events under an active grab on the root
  (Xplugin windows belong to the X server, AppKit dragging is not
  available), moving/resizing the frame with resize_frame like the
  title-bar drag and grow box; motion is coalesced only while the next
  queued event is motion too. Honours WM_NORMAL_HINTS min/max/inc, keeps
  the opposite edge fixed, keeps a 28 px top strip on screen and the top
  edge below the menu bar; ends if the window is minimized, hidden or made
  fullscreen under it. Ignored if the button is already up.
* Frameless windows (Motif decorations = 0, no title bar), from the
  passive grab on the client window: a button 1 press within
  wm_frameless_resize_border (default 5 px, 0 = off) of the left, right or
  bottom edge, 3 px of the top edge (Steam's top bar menus live below
  it), or 16 px of a corner resizes the window and never reaches the
  client; Cmd-Option-drag moves it from anywhere (Option is Mode_switch,
  an XKB group shift the press event does not carry, so the server's
  current state is asked for when Cmd is down). Every other press is
  replayed to the client as before. The activating click goes through
  (click-through), so dragging an inactive window by its own title bar is
  one gesture.
    defaults write org.steamarm.X11 wm_frameless_resize_border -int 8
* Double click on a frameless title bar (two move requests that name a
  button, as SDL3 sends them, and never moved, within
  com.apple.mouse.doubleClickThreshold) and on a quartz-wm title bar run
  System Settings' AppleActionOnDoubleClick (Zoom/Fill -> zoom, Minimize,
  None) instead of always minimizing; AppleMiniaturizeOnDoubleClick = NO
  in X11's own domain still turns the title bar one off (the global key is
  not read for that: System Settings sets it to 0 for Zoom and Fill).
  Chromium (button 0) handles its own. Pref to turn off the frameless one:
    defaults write org.steamarm.X11 wm_moveresize_double_click -bool false
* _NET_WM_STATE: MAXIMIZED_HORZ/VERT requests from inside a managed window
  apply to it (Chromium's caption buttons), and the pair counts as one
  request (a toggle no longer undoes itself); _NET_WM_STATE_ABOVE (keep
  above -> AppleWM floating level); _NET_WM_STATE_FOCUSED on the focused
  window (SDL3 takes input focus from it). The property is only rewritten
  when it changes, not on every frame change of a drag.
* _NET_FRAME_EXTENTS (0, 0, title bar height, 0) so SDL3/Chromium place
  decorated windows where they asked.
* _NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW with source indication 2 (pager) also un-minimizes /
  un-hides; applications (1: Steam's SDL_RaiseWindow on notifications) and
  old clients (0) only get focus, as before.
* Integer prefs no longer go through BOOL, which is bool on arm64 and read
  every value as 1 (wm_auto_quit_timeout, wm_frameless_resize_border).

